+```text
+db14cb1ef39da6277ec4edcd9988a17d38d8bc0062edca244af1155b820282eb  box/twopoint-batch-20260903/twopoint_order_batch.py
+d8750d4e512645366e9e0c53153484eb5daa9c785434c1cc59658986d0ab138c  box/twopoint-batch-20260903/shape.py
+f42e463a190f4c2fbdc2bade7e33edb6554018c5831e07844f4276f181b458ae  box/twopoint-batch-20260903/results.json
+3eca97dd36f2eb4b41d8473d67566d3db8359aee4a286a3081f1d9bce1fd8d4a  box/twopoint-batch-20260903/summary.tsv
+```
+
+No ledger files were edited.  I did not open the prohibited in-progress lane
+reports.
+
+## Generator
+
+Implemented `twopoint_order_batch.py` as a fresh dispatcher over the 17-group /
+18-row target list of `post-poly-census` §5.1.
+
+For each descended row `(n',m';M2',V2';k)` the driver computes
+
+```text
+d2' = gcd(n',m') = K,     d3' = gcd(d2',M2'),
+d'  = m'/K,               e'  = n'/K,
+u'  = d2' - V2',          v'  = V2',
+R   = n' - M2' - 1.
+```
+
+Root counts used in the order bound:
+
+```text
+high polynomial: e' V2' in the y=0 part, e' u' in the split part
+low polynomial:  d' V2' in the y=0 part, d' u' in the split part
+```
+
+The charged closed form from `prop55k` §2.4 was used:
+
+```text
+delta2' = -(k+1)/R
+delta1' = (k+1) * ((e'+d')u' - R) / (R((e'+d')V2' - 1)).
+```
+
+Important correction to the prompt wording: the charged formula gives
+`delta2'=-1` iff `R=k+1`, not iff `R=1`.  The promoted
+`(28,20;25;3;k=1)` has `R=2`; all 18 rows in this batch satisfy
+`R=k+1`.  I used the charged formula and recorded the check instead of forcing
+the inconsistent shorthand.
+
+The common coefficient bound is
+
+```text
+B = V2' delta1' + u' delta2',
+coefficient at h-deficit i has ord >= i B.
+```
+
+Invariant audit for the full target list:
+
+| source | descended | d2' | d3' | e' | d' | u' | R | delta1' | A1 | endpoint |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| `(64,48)` | `(16,12;13;3;k=1)` | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 1 | 2=2 | 1/4 | 4 | (12) |
+| `(75,50)` V2=2 | `(15,10;11;2;k=2)` | 5 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 3=3 | 4/3 | 3 | (12) |
+| `(75,50)` V2=3 | `(15,10;11;3;k=2)` | 5 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 3=3 | 1/2 | 2 | (13) |
+| `(84,56)` | `(21,14;18;5;k=1)` | 7 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 2=2 | 1/3 | 3 | (12) |
+| `(112,80)` | `(28,20;25;3;k=1)` | 4 | 1 | 7 | 5 | 1 | 2=2 | 2/7 | 7 | (12) |
+| `(125,75)` | `(25,15;21;2;k=2)` | 5 | 1 | 5 | 3 | 3 | 3=3 | 7/5 | 5 | (12) |
+| `(132,88)` | `(33,22;30;8;k=1)` | 11 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 2=2 | 1/3 | 3 | (12) |
+| `(147,98)` | `(21,14;15;6;k=4)` | 7 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 5=5 | 0 | 1 | (12),(13) |
+| `(160,112)` | `(40,28;37;3;k=1)` | 4 | 1 | 10 | 7 | 1 | 2=2 | 3/10 | 10 | (12) |
+| `(168,112)` drop1 | `(24,16;18;7;k=4)` | 8 | 2 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 5=5 | 0 | 1 | (12),(13) |
+| `(175,100)` | `(35,20;31;2;k=2)` | 5 | 1 | 7 | 4 | 3 | 3=3 | 10/7 | 7 | (12) |
+| `(175,125)` | `(35,25;31;3;k=2)` | 5 | 1 | 7 | 5 | 2 | 3=3 | 3/5 | 5 | (13) |
+| `(180,120)` drop1 | `(45,30;42;11;k=1)` | 15 | 3 | 3 | 2 | 4 | 2=2 | 1/3 | 3 | (12) |
+| `(180,144)` | `(30,24;25;4;k=3)` | 6 | 1 | 5 | 4 | 2 | 4=4 | 2/5 | 5 | (12) |
+| `(189,126)` drop1 | `(27,18;21;8;k=4)` | 9 | 3 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 5=5 | 0 | 1 | (12),(13) |
+| `(192,128)` | `(24,16;17;2;k=5)` | 8 | 1 | 3 | 2 | 6 | 6=6 | 8/3 | 3 | (12) |
+| `(196,56)` | `(49,14;46;4;k=1)` | 7 | 1 | 7 | 2 | 3 | 2=2 | 5/7 | 7 | (12) |
+| `(200,120)` | `(50,30;47;7;k=1)` | 10 | 1 | 5 | 3 | 3 | 2=2 | 2/5 | 5 | (12) |
+
+Here `R=a=b` displays `R` and `k+1`; every row has equality.  Rows with
+`delta1'=0` were still emitted where the charged two-point A/B chart had a
+finite, licensed form; the zero first-radius value is recorded and not hidden.
+
+The h-adic Jacobian equations are generated by the identity
+
+```text
+J(a h^r, b h^s)
+  = h^(r+s) J(a,b)
+  + h^(r+s-1)(s b J(a,h) + r a J(h,b)),
+```
+
+followed by monic Euclidean division by `h` in the `y`/`pi` variable.  The
+`h^0` remainder is equated to `c*x^k` (or `c*gamma^k` in the K16 naming), with
+Rabinowitsch saturation `T*c-1`.  The generated Singular rings run over either
+`Q` or `GF(p)` with `dp` order, and each generated ring first runs
+
+```text
+<c, T*c-1>       -> [1]     wrapper-empty control
+<c-1, T*c-1>     -> nonunit wrapper-nonempty control
+```
+
+## Top face and gauges
+
+Top-face policy:
+
+```text
+u'=1:  fixed y^V2'(y-x)
+u'=2:  fixed y^V2'(y^2-x^2)
+u'>=3: not licensed for new rows here; run/count D1-only with monic y^K fixed
+```
+
+The only u'>=3 fixed-top exception is the Moh/Appendix-II control
+`(15,10;11;2;k=2)`, where the charged compiler licenses the printed
+`y^2(y-x)^3` control and requires `[1]`.  For all new u'>=3 rows, a fixed
+`y^V(y-x)^u` kill would be a slice, so it is not used as a theorem.
+
+K16 rows use the generalized Theorem-1.2 flag basis derived from the independent
+t=2 generator:
+
+```text
+h = y A + b4,  A = y B + b3,  B = y(y-x) + b1 y + b2.
+```
+
